title: The code behind this week
subtitle: week-23-service-networking-lattice - what each file does, and how big it actually is
width: 1080
---
week-23-service-networking-lattice/
│
├── terraform/
│   ├── environments/dev/            # WHAT this environment is
│   │   ├── main.tf           65     # HCP backend, provider pins, one module
│   │   │                            # call. service_auth_type is a VARIABLE,
│   │   │                            # because test 5 flips it to NONE
│   │   ├── variables.tf      14
│   │   └── outputs.tf        32     # service DNS, both function names
│   │
│   └── modules/lattice/             # HOW it is built -- 24 resources
│       ├── network.tf        98     # VPC, two subnets, ONE security group
│       │                            # shared by both callers on purpose.
│       │                            # No NAT, no internet gateway.
│       ├── lattice.tf       138     # service network, service, listener,
│       │                            # target group, and BOTH auth policies
│       ├── compute.tf       260     # two caller Lambdas, the backend, and
│       │                            # three IAM roles
│       ├── variables.tf      46
│       └── outputs.tf        43
│
├── lambda/
│   ├── backend/handler.py    32     # the protected service. Performs NO
│   │                                # authorisation of its own -- that is
│   │                                # the entire argument
│   └── client/handler.py    190     # the caller. Signs with SigV4, forces
│                                    # IPv4, sends UNSIGNED-PAYLOAD. Ten
│                                    # self-tests, all earned the hard way
│
└── scripts/
    ├── test_auth.sh         149     # the six tests, in order, pass/fail
    └── cleanup.sh            76     # teardown verification

The two callers are 2 of those 24 resources and differ in exactly one
attribute: the IAM role attached to them.
